The prototype exposed a fatal leakage: a high-cut coloring gives a valid contraction certificate via Lemma 1, and a basic MaxCut local search already solved all 20/20 tested instances at \(n=96\). That rules out this inverse-split distribution for Track A even though spectral and odd-cycle heuristics failed. I’m checking whether this is merely a parameter issue or an inherent conflict between inverse splitting, the answer cap, and the paper’s rank equivalence before deciding whether the paper must be rejected.
