The partial module’s core construction is sound, but the audit found three concrete issues before oracle testing: the canonical invariant accidentally counted one endpoint twice; rare low-Hamming cross edges could invalidate the claimed compact route on an unlimited seed stream; and `escalate()` lengthened the answer before exhausting fixed-length hardness. I’m correcting those and adding an executable audit of the intended parity-kernel route.
