codex
Built a Track B affine Rank-Cut generator based on the paper’s Section 3 auxiliary problem. The paper confirms contraction witnesses are unordered edge sets—not reconfiguration sequences—and gives \(2^{O(k^2)}\) FPT algorithms for Rank-Cut. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1305.2743)

Deterministic results:

- G1–G8 pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000.
- Four heuristic attacks: 0/8 each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, median 20,661 bit operations.
- Compact parity-kernel route: 8/8, 204 operations.
- Additional audit: 4,000 generated instances verified.

G9 and the oracle hardening remain unscored: all bare, hinted, and placebo calls returned OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The result is therefore not yet submit-ready.

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/gen_1305_2743.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

A renewed `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` is required to finish Step 4 and G9.
