   224	## Caveats
   225	
   226	- G4 samples uniformly from affine polynomials already satisfying the terminal
   227	  orientation. It measures that declared prior only; it does not contradict the
   228	  guaranteed kernel recovery or rule out a better nonuniform attack.
   229	- The affine `F_2` labels and polynomial witness language are this benchmark's
   230	  restriction of the paper's native Rank-Cut object. They are not a construction
   231	  claimed by the paper, although verification still performs the paper's exact
   232	  cut and graphic-rank test rather than replacing it with a surrogate.
   233	- This is Track B because a fast reference algorithm succeeds by construction.
   234	  The paper's FPT theorems are not evidence that this planted distribution is
   235	  Track-A hard, and no such claim is made.
   236	- No SAT/SMT encoding, optimized max-flow package, or full implementation of the
   237	  paper's important-separator algorithm was tested. The inexpensive exact
   238	  Ford–Fulkerson/elimination route is already the relevant successful baseline.
   239	- `canonical_key` uses terminal-rooted colour refinement followed by affine
   240	  normalization. Generated instances individualized in every audit, but the
   241	  fallback for a hand-edited instance with unresolved twins is weaker than full
   242	  graph isomorphism.
   243	- Most importantly, the four-vendor bare/hinted/placebo evidence is absent. The
   244	  existing transcripts prove only that the configured key was exhausted.
