codex
Built a verified `TRACK = "B"` Rank-Cut generator based on the paper’s central reduction and exact graphic-rank certificate formulation. The prior “reconfiguration sequence” hypothesis was incorrect because contraction order is irrelevant.

Deliverables:

- [gen_1305_2743.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/gen_1305_2743.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/README.md)
- [bare hardening transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1305.2743/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000 from \(2^{23}\) candidates.
- Five attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 8/8, median 20,661 operations.
- Compact invariant route: 8/8, 204 operations.
- Bare oracle hardening: 0/3 solved across OpenAI and Google; `easy` ships.
- Structural hint: 1/3 solved.
- Placebo arm: unscored because the OpenRouter key reached its total limit; all four retries returned HTTP 403. Consequently, `hinted − placebo` remains undefined and is documented honestly.

The theorem and algorithm basis comes from the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1305.2743).
